data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":91,"item_id":"rs_0309cb632c6daec4016acc2aca97948196acfe6a362c596c26","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Considering SSR form implementation**\n\nI'm thinking about implementing server-side rendered forms that are simple, accessible, and robust, without needing frontend JavaScript. I want to make sure I handle blank submissions with post form redirects and status 400 alerts. It looks like I won't need an API, as I can test my own HTTP setup. I also need to consider using SQLite for synchronization and ensuring proper CSS handling, with tests that use a temporary database without cluttering the repository."}

